# App
NODE_ENV=development
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_LOCALE=en-CA
NEXT_PUBLIC_SEASON=2026/27

# Database — Neon Postgres (or any Postgres URL)
# Deploy path uses Neon; local SQLite file:./dev.db is no longer used.
# For local: use a Neon free DB, or a local Postgres URL.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/neondb?sslmode=require"

# Auth.js
# Default is localhost for QA. AUTH_TRUST_HOST=true + trustHost lets the
# incoming Host / x-forwarded-host / x-forwarded-proto win, so
# http://localhost:3000 and an https tunnel (trycloudflare / loca.lt)
# share one process. Middleware forwards Host as x-forwarded-host when
# it is not localhost. Cookies are Secure only on https.
# Tunnel-only users can pin:
#   AUTH_URL=https://your-subdomain.trycloudflare.com
#   AUTH_TRUST_HOST=false
# Production (Vercel): AUTH_TRUST_HOST=true, a strong AUTH_SECRET, and
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL = the real production URL. AUTH_URL is optional;
# if set, it must be that same real URL — not https://example.com.
# Loopback and IANA example.* AUTH_URL values are ignored so request Host wins.
# AUTH_SECRET is required — without it every /api/auth/* route 500s
# (MissingSecret) and demo login lands on ?error=NoSession.
AUTH_SECRET=generate-a-long-random-string
AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
AUTH_TRUST_HOST=true

# Optional Google OAuth (demo works without these)
# AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=
# AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=

# Live scores + injuries use ESPN public JSON — no key required.
# Optional later (not wired): API-Sports free-tier key if ESPN is blocked.
# API_SPORTS_KEY=

# Forgot-password codes and optional Sign-in codes (NOT a code at every sign-in).
# Minimum for friends today — email:
#   RESEND_API_KEY=
#   RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=Survive Sunday <noreply@yourdomain.com>
# From must be a sender Resend has verified (add a domain at resend.com).
# Do NOT use onboarding@resend.dev in production — that only delivers to the
# Resend login email, not friends. If either key is missing, the live site
# now says so in plain English instead of failing silently.
# Optional texts if a friend saved a cell:
#   TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
#   TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
#   TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=+1XXXXXXXXXX
# Local/dev without keys: the code is printed in the terminal and shown on
# the reset page. Production never shows the code in the browser.
#
# The same Resend / Twilio keys send pool emails and texts.
# Account → Notification preferences is one choice: Email / SMS / both / none.
# GAME notices (reminders, you’re out) respect that choice. Password-reset
# codes always send when requested (SECURITY — never blocked by none).
# Outbound GAME / Admin-alert traffic is gated by:
#   NOTIFY_MODE=dryrun | allowlist | live
# Preview/local default is dryrun (nothing sent; NotificationSend logs dry_run).
# Production default is allowlist until an Administrator sets live.
#   NOTIFY_ALLOWLIST=robert@example.com,+1XXXXXXXXXX
# Optional: cron auth for /api/cron/missing-pick-reminders and
# /api/cron/ensure-week (Vercel also sends x-vercel-cron: 1).
# Ensure-week runs daily at 16:30 UTC (12:30 p.m. ET) and 23:45 UTC
# (7:45 p.m. ET): pick backup copy, lock effects, ESPN sync.
# (Hobby Vercel only allows once-per-day crons — do not use */15.)
# CRON_SECRET=
